## On the job {.unnumbered}

::: callout-important
## Why this matters day to day

Every engagement survey, exit interview scorecard, interview rating,
and pulse check in your organisation is ordinal data. The habit of
averaging Likert items and running a t-test or linear regression is
extremely common and usually harmless when categories are numerous and
responses spread out — and genuinely misleading exactly when survey
data tends to look in practice: few categories, bunched toward the
positive end. Checking your data's shape before choosing, rather than
defaulting to the familiar tool, is the actual skill here.
:::

